### Project-Victory — playtest pela API (extensão REST Client do VS Code)
### PV-QA-010. Ordem = docs/playtest/ROTEIRO-PLAYTEST.md. Sem Swagger no projeto.
### Antes: Jwt:Key nos user-secrets (developer-guide/guides/configuracao-local.md) e
###        dotnet run --project src/ProjectVictory.API
### EXEMPLO: e-mail e senha abaixo são genéricos, só para teste local. Troque o e-mail a cada playtest.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5250
@email = jogador.exemplo@example.com
@password = SenhaDeExemplo123
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}
# characterId vem da resposta do enter (objeto JSON); o 3c só resolve depois do passo 4.
@characterId = {{enter.response.body.$.characterId}}
@runtimeId = {{enter.response.body.$.runtimeId}}
@huntId = {{hunt.response.body.$.huntId}}
# Atualize à mão a cada encounter: comece por encounter.id do "hunt"; depois de uma vitória use nextEncounterId.
@encounterId = {{hunt.response.body.$.encounter.id}}

### 1. Registro (público) -> 200, Id da conta
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. Login (público) -> 200 { accountId, token }
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 3. Criar personagem -> 200, Id do personagem (Knight | Paladin | Sorcerer | Druid | Monk)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/character
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Exemplo",
  "characterClass": "Knight"
}

### 3b. Listar personagens -> level, experience, title
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/character
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3c. Inventário (kit inicial e loot) — rode depois do passo 4 (enter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/{{characterId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Entrar no mundo -> 200 { runtimeId, ... }
# @name enter
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/game/enter
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Heartbeat (repita a cada 20-30 s durante a Hunt) -> status "Online"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/game/heartbeat
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Iniciar Hunt na Spider Cave -> 200 { huntId, encounter }; 2a Hunt -> 409; área desconhecida -> 400
# @name hunt
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/hunt/execute
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "characterId": "{{characterId}}",
  "runtimeId": "{{runtimeId}}",
  "huntArea": "Spider Cave"
}

### 7. Atacar (repita; leia turns[], combatState, nextEncounterId)
# @name attack
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/hunt/attack
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encounterId": "{{encounterId}}"
}

### 8. Configurar poções (1-100 ou null) -> 200 appliesFrom "NextTurn"; inválido -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/hunt/supplies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "characterId": "{{characterId}}",
  "healthPotionBelowPercent": 60,
  "manaPotionBelowPercent": 40
}

### 9. Cura por spell: automática (turno kind "UseHealingSpell" na resposta do ataque). Sem requisição própria.

### 10. Analyzer em tempo real -> hasActiveHunt true, analyzer {...}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/hunt/analyzer/{{characterId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Sair da Hunt -> reason "Manual", returnedToCity true; repetir -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/hunt/leave
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "huntId": "{{huntId}}"
}

### 12. Histórico do Analyzer -> [{ huntId, endReason, endedAt, analyzer }]
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/hunt/analyzer/{{characterId}}/history
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Logout -> returnCity "Victoria"; heartbeat seguinte -> status "LoggedOut"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/game/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Administrador do XP rate ---
### Pré-requisito: o accountId desta conta em user-secrets e API reiniciada:
###   dotnet user-secrets set "Admin:Accounts:0" "<accountId>" --project src/ProjectVictory.API
### Jogador comum -> 403; sem token -> 401.

### A1. Ler XP rate -> { value, configuredValue, isOverridden, changedAt, maximum }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/xp-rate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A2. Alterar XP rate (0 < value <= 100) -> 200; inválido -> 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/xp-rate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": 2.5
}
